;; Files `ocamlc -c` compiles alone (O3's level) whose typed or Lambda dump is a compiler error, by mode (bin/repr-ocaml
;; types|lambda|dumps, doc/ocaml/SPEC.md 14.3), with the class. Read with the Clojure reader.
;;   :shadowed -- the unit was compiled while the .cmi of a later unit of its directory did not exist yet; the dump, run
;;   after every unit of the corpus is compiled, finds that .cmi first and it shadows a standard library module
;;   (testsuite/tests/backtrace/lazy.ml is a unit `Lazy` without `force`). An artifact of the order, not of the dump;
;;   a dependency-order build (OC41 (b), OC51) removes it.
{:types {"testsuite/tests/backtrace/backtrace2.ml" :shadowed}
 :lambda {"testsuite/tests/backtrace/backtrace2.ml" :shadowed}}
